{{also|Mund}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|mund|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem|en}}. Cognate with German {{term|Mund|lang=de}}, {{term|Munt||legal protection|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mʊnd/|/mʌnd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[hand]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} [[security]], granted by a king or earl, the violation of which was punished by a [[fine]] (a [[mundbyrd]])
# [[protection|Protection]], [[guardianship]].

===Anagrams===
* [[UNDM#English|UNDM]]

